"English (United States) News_Detail (https://www.sec.or.th/EN/Pages/News_Detail.aspx?SECID=12047)\nciteturn33view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.sec.or.th/EN/Pages/News_Detail.aspx?SECID=12047\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 67\nL0: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL1: \nL2: [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: cite0†Turn on more accessible mode L5: \nL6: cite0†Turn off more accessible mode L7: \nL8: cite1†Sign In L9: \nL10: cite2†Image L11: \nL12: Header Template\nL13: \nL14: [Input]\nL15: \nL16:   * cite3†Home L17:   * >  cite0†News/Market Data L18:   * >  cite4†SEC News L19:   * >  cite5†News Detail L20: \nL21: [Input]\nL22: \nL23: [Input]\nL24: \nL25: SEC News\nL26: \nL27: * * *\nL28: SEC issues warning about access restriction of Bybit, 1000X, CoinEx, OKX, and XT.COM platforms on 28 June 2025 to protect investors and prevent illegal platforms from being used as money laundering channels\nL29: \nL30: Thursday 29 May 2025 | No. 134 / 2025\nL31: Bangkok, 29 May 2025 – Pursuant to the Royal Decree on Measures for the Prevention and Suppression of Technological Crimes (No. 2) B.E. 2568 (2025), effective since 13 April 2025, the Ministry of Digital Economy and Society (MDES) is authorized to restrict access to unlicensed digital asset trading platforms.\nL32: Recently, the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) has conducted investigations and found that Bybit .com (https://www. bybit .com), 1000x .live (https://www. 1000x.live), CoinEx (https://www.coinex.com/), OKX (www.okx. com/th), and XT.COM (www.xt.com) had provided services of digital asset trading platforms without license.\nL33: The SEC therefore filed criminal complaints with the Economic Crime Suppression Division of the Royal Thai Police for offenses liable to be unlicensed digital asset business operations under the Emergency Decree on Digital Asset Businesses B.E. 2561 (2018) to pursue legal action.\nL34: To safeguard investors and prevent unlicensed digital asset trading platforms from being exploited as channels for money laundering, in line with the intent of the Royal Decree on Measures for the Prevention and Suppression of Technological Crimes (No. 2) B.E. 2568 (2025), the SEC has reported these platforms to the MDES. The MDES will restrict public access to them starting 28 June 2025.\nL35: In this regard, the SEC advises investors currently using these platforms to take steps to secure their assets before the access restriction takes effect.\nL36: The SEC advises the public and investors to be cautious when using services of unlicensed digital asset business operators; otherwise, they will not be legally protected and will be at risk of being scammed, as well as facing money laundering risks. The list of licensed business operators is available at https://www.sec.or.th and the SEC Check First application.\nL37: Additionally, the names of persons who are not regulated business operators under the SEC’s supervision can be verified on the Investor Alert List via this link:  cite6†https://market.sec.or.th/public/idisc/en/InvestorAlert†market.sec.or.th L38: Furthermore, to report any leads concerning suspicious activities, please contact the SEC Complaint Center via Hotline 1207, or the SEC Facebook page: “สำนักงาน กลต.” or the SEC Live Chat on the SEC website, for further in-depth investigation.\nL39: \nL40: * * *\nL41: ###### Documents\nL42: \nL43:   * SHARE :\nL44:   *   *   *   *   * * * *\nL45: ###### Related News\nL46: SEC imposes civil sanctions on three offenders for manipulating the price or trading volume of NCL shares\nL47: SEC outlines progress on key measures to drive a high-quality “Thai investment market”\nL48: SEC seeks public comments on proposed principles for supervising stablecoin transactions to mitigate financial fraud risks\nL49: SEC imposes civil sanctions on four offenders for manipulating the trading volume of digital asset named SIX Network\nL50: SEC Board approves principles for enhancing the supervision of stablecoin transactions conducted through digital asset business operators\nL51: * * *\nL52: \nL53: Building Confidence in the Capital Market\nL54: NEWS cite7†Image Securities and Exchange Commission Corporate Communication and Investor Service Department Tel. (66)2033-9502-5 E-mail: press@sec.or.th cite8†Image L55: No. 134 / 2025 Thursday 29 May 2025\nL56: SEC issues warning about access restriction of Bybit, 1000X, CoinEx, OKX, and XT.COM platforms on 28 June 2025 to protect investors and prevent illegal platforms from being used as money laundering channels\nL57: Bangkok, 29 May 2025 – Pursuant to the Royal Decree on Measures for the Prevention and Suppression of Technological Crimes (No. 2) B.E. 2568 (2025), effective since 13 April 2025, the Ministry of Digital Economy and Society (MDES) is authorized to restrict access to unlicensed digital asset trading platforms.\nL58: Recently, the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) has conducted investigations and found that Bybit .com (https://www. bybit .com), 1000x .live (https://www. 1000x.live), CoinEx (https://www.coinex.com/), OKX (www.okx. com/th), and XT.COM (www.xt.com) had provided services of digital asset trading platforms without license.\nL59: The SEC therefore filed criminal complaints with the Economic Crime Suppression Division of the Royal Thai Police for offenses liable to be unlicensed digital asset business operations under the Emergency Decree on Digital Asset Businesses B.E.\nL60: 2561 (2018) to pursue legal action. To safeguard investors and prevent unlicensed digital asset trading platforms from being exploited as channels for money laundering, in line with the intent of the Royal Decree on Measures for the Prevention and Suppression of Technological Crimes (No. 2) B.E. 2568 (2025), the SEC has reported these platforms to the MDES.\nL61: The MDES will restrict public access to them starting 28 June 2025.   In this regard, the SEC advises investors currently using these platforms to take steps to secure their assets before the access restriction takes effect. The SEC advises the public and investors to be cautious when using services of unlicensed digital asset business operators; otherwise, they will not be legally protected and will be at risk of being scammed, as well as facing money laundering risks.\nL62: The list of licensed business operators is available at https://www.sec.or.th and the SEC Check First application.\nL63: Additionally, the names of persons who are not regulated business operators under the SEC’s supervision can be verified on the Investor Alert List via this link:  cite6†https://market.sec.or.th/public/idisc/en/InvestorAlert†market.sec.or.th Furthermore, to report any leads concerning suspicious activities, please contact the SEC Complaint Center via Hotline 1207, or the SEC Facebook page: “สำนักงาน กลต.” or the SEC Live Chat on the SEC website, for further in-depth investigation.\nL64: * * *\nL65: \nL66: [Input]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEnglish (United States) News_Detail (https://www.sec.or.th/EN/Pages/News_Detail.aspx?SECID=12048)\nciteturn33view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.sec.or.th/EN/Pages/News_Detail.aspx?SECID=12048\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 66\nL0: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL1: \nL2: [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: cite0†Turn on more accessible mode L5: \nL6: cite0†Turn off more accessible mode L7: \nL8: cite1†Sign In L9: \nL10: cite2†Image L11: \nL12: Header Template\nL13: \nL14: [Input]\nL15: \nL16:   * cite3†Home L17:   * >  cite0†News/Market Data L18:   * >  cite4†SEC News L19:   * >  cite5†News Detail L20: \nL21: [Input]\nL22: \nL23: [Input]\nL24: \nL25: SEC News\nL26: \nL27: * * *\nL28: SEC urges investors to secure their assets before access restrictions of Bybit, 1000X, CoinEx, OKX and XT.COM platforms take effect on 28 June 2025\nL29: \nL30: Thursday 26 June 2025 | No. 160 / 2025\nL31: Bangkok, 26 June 2025 – Pursuant to the Royal Decree on Measures for the Prevention and Suppression of Technological Crime (No. 2) B.E. 2568 (2025), effective since 13 April 2025, the Ministry of Digital Economy and Society (MDES) is authorized to restrict access to unauthorized digital asset trading platforms.\nL32: On 29 May 2025, the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) submitted information on such unauthorized platforms, namely (1) Bybit.com, (2) 1000x.live, (3) CoinEx, (4) OKX, and (5) XT.COM to the MDES*. The MDES will proceed to restrict access to these platforms on 28 June 2025, in order to protect investors and prevent unlicensed digital asset trading platforms from being exploited as channels for money laundering by wrongdoers, in line with the legislative intent.\nL33: The SEC urges investors who use these platforms to consider withdrawing or transferring their assets from the platforms before 28 June 2025 to protect their interests and prevent any potential impact that may arise after the platforms are blocked.\nL34: The SEC advises the public and investors to be cautious when using services of unlicensed DA business operators. The list of unlicensed business operators is available at cite6†https://market.sec.or.th/public/idisc/en/InvestorAlert†market.sec.or.th . Additionally, the list of licensed business operators is available at www.sec.or.th and the SEC Check First application.\nL35: Furthermore, to report any leads concerning suspicious activities, please contact the SEC Complaint Center via Hotline 1207, or the SEC Facebook page: “สำนักงาน กลต.” or the SEC Live Chat on the SEC website, for further in-depth investigation.\nL36: * * *\nL37: \nL38: Remark:\nL39: \nL40: * SEC News No. 134/2025, headlined: “SEC issues warning about blocking access to Bybit, 1000X, CoinEx, OKX, and XT.COM platforms on 28 June 2025 to protect investors and prevent illegal platforms from being used as money laundering channels,” released on 29 May 2025: cite7†https://www.sec.or.th/EN/Pages/News_Detail.aspx?SECID=12047 L41: ###### Documents\nL42: \nL43:   * SHARE :\nL44:   *   *   *   *   * * * *\nL45: ###### Related News\nL46: SEC imposes civil sanctions on three offenders for manipulating the price or trading volume of NCL shares\nL47: SEC outlines progress on key measures to drive a high-quality “Thai investment market”\nL48: SEC seeks public comments on proposed principles for supervising stablecoin transactions to mitigate financial fraud risks\nL49: SEC imposes civil sanctions on four offenders for manipulating the trading volume of digital asset named SIX Network\nL50: SEC Board approves principles for enhancing the supervision of stablecoin transactions conducted through digital asset business operators\nL51: * * *\nL52: \nL53: Building Confidence in the Capital Market\nL54: NEWS cite8†Image Securities and Exchange Commission Corporate Communication and Investor Service Department Tel. (66)2033-9502-5 E-mail: press@sec.or.th cite9†Image L55: No. 160 / 2025 Thursday 26 June 2025\nL56: SEC urges investors to secure their assets before access restrictions of Bybit, 1000X, CoinEx, OKX and XT.COM platforms take effect on 28 June 2025\nL57: Bangkok, 26 June 2025 – Pursuant to the Royal Decree on Measures for the Prevention and Suppression of Technological Crime (No. 2) B.E. 2568 (2025), effective since 13 April 2025, the Ministry of Digital Economy and Society (MDES) is authorized to restrict access to unauthorized digital asset trading platforms.\nL58: On 29 May 202